ithub.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-08T17:16:39Z","updated_at":"2026-06-08T17:18:34Z","body":"Rebased and tested again, it works as expected. \r\n\r\n> I think it'd be better to add a reset button next to the debug draw popup button and remove the 'Display Normal' option.\r\n\r\nI'd prefer the UX of the dropdown to be 1:1 with the one found in the editor, so that we don't break users' muscle memory.\r\n\r\n> It'd be also really helpful to have a toggle button to show and hide collision shapes. This PR doesn't need to add it though.\r\n\r\nThis requires https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/2072 to be implemented first.\r\n\r\n> - This button should be invisible if 3D stuff is disabled in the editor feature profile (the same way as 3D button) - for 2D this button does nothing.\r\n\r\nDone. I also fixed the icon being tinted while the dropdown is open.\r\n\r\n> - Not sure, but could existing code be reused without duplication in game_view_plugin?\r\n\r\nI refactored the code as per @KoBeWi's suggestions. There should be less duplicated code now.\r\n\r\n> The debug draw options button shouldn't be between camera button and camera options. Maybe put it next to mute button?\r\n\r\nI moved the debug draw mode dropdown to the right of the Mute button.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4651527147/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocke